A '''Super Nerd''' (Japanese: '''{{tt|理科系|りかけい}}のおとこ''' ''Science Man''; in [[Generation I]], also known as '''りかけい''' ''Science'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that first debuted in the [[Generation I]] games. They are generally depicted as skinny young men with long hair and glasses, and are grown-up male {{tc|School Kid}}s.<ref name="NOM 2000-07" /> In {{2v2|HeartGold|SoulSilver}}, they are accompanied by a remote-controlled robotic {{p|Pikachu}} holding a {{i|Poké Ball}}.

They generally use a combination of {{t|Poison}}- and {{type|Electric}} Pokémon based on inanimate objects, except those in the [[Cinnabar Gym]], who specialize in {{type|Fire}}s instead. 

In [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!|Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!]], Super Nerds battled outside of [[Gym]]s will award three {{i|Poké Ball}}s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated.

In [[Pokémon Stadium]], they are referred to as '''Nerds''' and specialize in Pokémon knowing {{m|Self-Destruct|Selfdestruct}} or {{m|Explosion}}.

